    "clinicalPearl": "Key takeaway: True Hutchinson's sign = pigment extension from nail onto proximal/lateral nail fold = acral lentiginous melanoma (increased melanocyte number). Pseudo-Hutchinson's = increased melanin only, no periungual extension, benign.",
